{% comment %}
  PRIME provisional layout (docs/analysis/smv-preparation-general-revision.md §4.2, L6-2c): computation of the unit base market values of agricultural land.
  LAM 2025 Book IV pp.114–115 lists the form; its layout (Annex IV-H) is loaded as content and is not reproduced here.
  DOMAIN VERIFICATION REQUIRED: its columns.
{% endcomment %}
<style>
  h1 { font-size: 12pt; text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 2px; }
  h2 { font-size: 9.5pt; margin: 8px 0 3px; }
  .lgu { text-align: center; font-weight: bold; }
  .sub { text-align: center; font-size: 9pt; margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .flag { text-align: center; font-weight: bold; letter-spacing: 1px; border: 1px solid #000; padding: 2px; margin: 4px 0; }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 0 0 6px; }
  td, th { border: 1px solid #000; padding: 2px 4px; font-size: 7.5pt; vertical-align: top; }
  th { background: #eee; font-weight: bold; text-align: left; }
  .num { text-align: right; white-space: nowrap; }
  .pre { white-space: pre-wrap; }
  .muted { color: #555; font-size: 7.5pt; }
  .sig { margin-top: 26px; width: 240px; border-top: 1px solid #000; text-align: center; font-size: 8.5pt; padding-top: 2px; display: inline-block; margin-right: 50px; }
  .foot { font-size: 7.5pt; margin-top: 6px; }
</style>
{% assign a = analysis %}
{% if lgu.name %}<div class="lgu">{{ lgu.name }}</div>{% endif %}{% if lgu.office %}<div class="sub">{{ lgu.office }}</div>{% endif %}
<h1>SMV FORM NO. 8 — COMPUTATION FOR THE UNIT BASE MARKET VALUE OF AGRICULTURAL LANDS</h1>
<div class="sub">Classification: {{ a.classification }}{% if a.use %} — {{ a.use }}{% endif %} · {{ a.marketAreas | join: ", " }} · Revision {{ a.revisionYear }}
 · base valuation date {% if a.baseValuationDate %}{{ a.baseValuationDate | date_ph }}{% else %}not set{% endif %}</div>
{% for w in a.warnings %}<div class="muted">{{ w }}</div>{% endfor %}

<h2>Table 1 — unit values from the lowest to the highest</h2>
<table><tr><th class="num">No.</th><th class="num">Adjusted unit value</th><th class="num">Rounded</th><th class="num">Interval %</th></tr>
  {% for v in values %}<tr><td class="num">{{ v.number }}</td><td class="num">{{ v.adjusted | money }}</td><td class="num">{{ v.rounded | money }}</td><td class="num">{{ v.interval }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
</table>
<div class="muted">Average interval: {{ a.averageInterval }}%. Ranges at ±{{ a.width }}%{% if a.widthEntered %} (entered by the assessor){% else %} (the average interval){% endif %}.</div>
<h2>Table 2 — ranges and the number of sales in each</h2>
<table><tr><th class="num">Range</th><th class="num">Low</th><th class="num">Mid</th><th class="num">High</th><th class="num">Frequency</th><th>Sub-class</th></tr>
  {% for r in ranges %}<tr><td class="num">{{ r.number }}</td><td class="num">{{ r.low | money }}</td><td class="num">{{ r.mid | money }}</td><td class="num">{{ r.high | money }}</td><td class="num">{{ r.frequency }}</td><td>{{ r.subClass }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
</table>
<h2>Table 3 — sub-classes and unit values, highest to lowest</h2>
<table><tr><th>Sub-class</th><th class="num">Rounded values</th><th class="num">Sales</th><th class="num">Proposed by computation</th><th class="num">Unit value adopted</th><th>Basis</th></tr>
  {% for g in groups %}<tr><td>{{ g.subClass }}</td><td class="num">{{ g.from | money }} – {{ g.to | money }}</td><td class="num">{{ g.sales }}</td>
    <td class="num">{% if g.proposed %}{{ g.proposed | money }}{% endif %}</td><td class="num">{% if g.adopted %}{{ g.adopted | money }}{% if g.adoptedAt == nil %} (not yet adopted){% endif %}{% endif %}</td><td>{{ g.basis }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
</table>
<div class="muted">Unit values {{ a.unit }}. PRIME computes the ranges by its stated reading of the annex steps (docs/analysis/smv-preparation-general-revision.md §9, L6-2b).</div>
<div class="sig">Prepared by</div><div class="sig">Noted by: Assessor</div>
<div class="foot">{{ form.title }} — form {{ form.code }} v{{ form.version }}. {{ form.legalBasis }}. Printed {{ issue.issuedAt | datetime_ph }}{% if issue.issuedBy %} by {{ issue.issuedBy }}{% endif %}.</div>
